nges in relational pattern and strength of input variables with ehealth acceptance.", "bbox": {"x": 849.3, "y": 1403.8, "width": 713.3, "height": 249.20000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Conclusions E-health is relatively a new phenomenon to the rural communities in developing countries. The overall success of this initiative, therefore, does not simply depend on its IT design and implementation rather large-scale users' acceptance as well. '2,18 This study attempts to explain the factors that influence rural end-users' acceptance of e-health and found SR as the most significantly influential factor followed by Adv, users' ATS, access to a cellphone and PSE.", "bbox": {"x": 849.9, "y": 1688.0, "width": 712.6999999999999, "height": 323.29999999999995}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MARY ANN LIEBERT, INC. • VOL. 25 NO. 3 • MARCH 2019 TELEMEDICINE and e-HEALTH 227", "bbox": {"x": 588.0, "y": 2100.9, "width": 974.5999999999999, "height": 25.59999999999991}}], "ms": 222.72}